is is far from the only impact that  Fujiwara has had on me and millions of  others because if you take a look  through this man CV it is absolutely  absurd and the amount of projects that  he has been involved in just boggles the  mind so for example he was the voice of  RINO and just about every Final Fantasy  7 project including the remake that was  just released but another very formative  role was that of mass use in both  iterations of Full Metal Alchemist being  the original anime and of course  Brotherhood and you know as much as I  have pretty incredibly strong opinions  on both of those series one of the great  constants of quality was the mass use  because fujiwara justice would be Oreo  did a supreme job of turning Hughes into  a gripping personality someone who you  really  that you could not live without and  going back an awfully long way to a  series I was watching in high school  which you know I'm 30 now so that was a  while ago but Fujiwara was also Holland  in Eureka Seven which blew my mind when  I found that out but when I think about  it in retrospect I can very clearly hear  his voice in my mind's delivering  Holland's science interestingly enough  for Japanese specific audiences though  Fujiwara voice was absolutely massive in  the dub scene as he was the actor who  would portray rub it down a genius  characters so for example Fujiwara was  Tony Stark  in the entire Japanese incarnation of  the Marvel Cinematic Universe as well as  all of his other characters like  Sherlock Holmes and here's something  really really strange it has no effect  on me I haven't even seen it but I just  thought it was interesting is that  apparently Fujiwara was also the voice  dubbing Cuba Gooding jr. in the People  vs OJ Simpson which essentially means it  alongside the Oreo and Mars Hughes  Fujiwara has also played OJ Simpson that  just goes to show the range of  performative depth that this man had and  back to the realm of games he was also  found favorite a